"""GlioStrata Snakemake workflow — main Snakefile.

Orchestrates the real L0->L7 chain as the code actually implements it today.
Every path is derived from `config`, so the same DAG runs against the full
TCGA-GBM cohort or against a tiny synthetic fixture.

    # what would run against the real cohort
    snakemake -n --cores 1 --snakefile workflow/Snakefile

    # offline fixture run (no network, no GDC) — this is what CI and
    # `make pipeline` use
    snakemake --cores 1 --snakefile workflow/Snakefile \
        --config source=synthetic cohort=fixture n_synthetic=12 \
                 with_expression=false verify_partition=false \
                 raw_root=.test/raw interim_root=.test/interim \
                 processed_root=.test/processed results_root=.test/results

    # the real thing (NETWORK: GDC REST API, ~1.2 GB expression download)
    snakemake --cores 4 --snakefile workflow/Snakefile

Honesty notes — read these before reading the DAG as a scientific claim:
  * L1 harmonize, L2 profile, L5 survival and L6 optimize are STUBS. Each rule
    file states exactly what its layer does and does not do.
  * L2 does not consume the L0 expression matrices, so those matrices are a
    top-level target rather than an input edge. The DAG does not assert
    dependencies the code does not have.
  * Several real modules exist ALONGSIDE those stubs and are NOT wired into the
    CLI pipeline, so they are absent from this DAG by design, not by oversight:
        src/gliostrata/prediction/cox.py        — real Cox models; L5 still
                                                  calls prediction/survival.py
        src/gliostrata/profiling/verhaak.py     — real Verhaak classifier; L2
                                                  still calls profiling/subtype.py
        src/gliostrata/profiling/deconvolve.py  — deconvolution; L2 still calls
                                                  profiling/{states,tme}.py
        src/gliostrata/optimization/bayes_opt.py— real BO; L6 still calls
                                                  optimization/bayesian.py
        scripts/download_cgga.py                — CGGA ingest, no rule yet
    Adding rules for them would imply they are in the pipeline. They are not.
    Wiring them is a change to src/gliostrata/cli.py, not to this workflow.
  * CIBERSORTx deconvolution is a MANUAL round trip through a web tool. The
    export rule exists (rules/export.smk) but nothing consumes its output, so
    it is outside `rule all`.
  * Only the `ingest_tcga_*` rules touch the network. Running with
    `source=synthetic` is guaranteed offline.

See docs/reproducibility.md for what is genuinely reproducible today.
"""

include: "rules/common.smk"
include: "rules/ingest.smk"
include: "rules/harmonize.smk"
include: "rules/profile.smk"
include: "rules/features.smk"
include: "rules/partition.smk"
include: "rules/optimize.smk"
include: "rules/handoff.smk"
include: "rules/export.smk"


rule all:
    """Full pipeline: L0 ingest -> L7 protocols, plus the partition guardrail."""
    input:
        # L0 — expression matrices are produced but not yet consumed by L2.
        expression_targets(),
        # L2 — profiled table is produced but not consumed by L3 (see features.smk).
        PROFILED,
        # L3/L6/L7 — the chain that is actually wired end to end.
        FEATURE_STORE,
        RANKED_CONFIGS,
        PROTOCOL_DIR,
    output:
        touch(PIPELINE_STAMP),


rule ingest:
    """L0 only — ingest the cohort (and expression matrices, if enabled)."""
    input:
        cohort_parquet(),
        expression_targets(),


rule features:
    """Everything up to and including the L3 feature store."""
    input:
        FEATURE_STORE,


rule partition_check:
    """Verify the frozen train/test partition still reproduces. Nothing else."""
    input:
        PARTITION_STAMP,


rule cibersortx:
    """Build the CIBERSORTx mixture file only (manual upload; see rules/export.smk)."""
    input:
        CIBERSORTX_MIXTURE,


rule clean_results:
    """Remove this cohort's derived results tree. Never touches data/raw or data/partitions."""
    params:
        results=RESULTS,
    shell:
        "rm -rf {params.results}"
